# scripts/restore-beads-local-files.sh reconstructs .beads/config.yaml,
# metadata.json, README.md and .gitignore by reading them back from THIS
# (private) repository's own git history (personal-cfo-fkt5.11's untracking
# commit). That history does not exist in the public go-live snapshot
# (docs/operations/public-launch-snapshot.md — a fresh, empty repository
# seeded by one squashed commit), so the script would do nothing useful
# there. export-ignore keeps `git archive` from carrying a script that only
# makes sense against the private archive's history (personal-cfo-apesm).
scripts/restore-beads-local-files.sh export-ignore

