# Maintainer-only bead-database backup tooling (personal-cfo-7d6k9, OWNER
# DIRECTIVE 2026-09-14): scripts/backup-beads.sh (the JSONL mirror),
# scripts/backup-dolt.sh (ADR 0064 §3's SECOND, independent backup — the
# Dolt database itself, with full history, to a file:// mirror on separate
# encrypted media; personal-cfo-es9ew), scripts/mirror-backup.sh, their
# regression tests, and their two runbooks exist only to back up the
# private bead task database and mirror this repository to private
# infrastructure. None of it is useful to someone using or auditing DohFlow,
# and beyond the private mirror repository name (the one reference to it
# worth publishing — ADR 0064's decision and reasoning — already uses a
# generic phrase instead), backup-dolt.sh also names a specific personal
# backup-volume model, a private backup-volume mount label, and makes an
# owner-account reference to a third-party hosted-database service —
# review finding F1 on PR #457.
# export-ignore keeps `git archive` from ever carrying any of it into the
# public repository; nothing is removed from this (private) repo's own
# working tree or history, and the CI shell-scripts job (a plain
# actions/checkout, not `git archive`) still runs all of it here — only the
# public snapshot's copy of that job sees fewer files, which its
# `scripts/*.sh` / `scripts/tests/*.test.sh` globs tolerate. (One residual,
# non-identifying mention of the backup-volume nickname remained in
# scripts/tests/git-hooks.test.sh, a file that keeps shipping — genericized
# in place rather than hidden, since that test has real public value.)
scripts/backup-beads.sh export-ignore
scripts/backup-dolt.sh export-ignore
scripts/mirror-backup.sh export-ignore
scripts/tests/backup-beads.test.sh export-ignore
scripts/tests/backup-dolt.test.sh export-ignore
docs/operations/beads-backup-and-restore.md export-ignore
docs/operations/repo-mirrors.md export-ignore

# Same rationale, three files the pass above missed on the first sweep
# (found by actually running the CI shell-scripts job's test loop against a
# `git archive` output, per this bead's own verification requirement):
# - scripts/launchd/app.dohflow.mirror-backup.plist configures a scheduled
#   launchd job that only exists on this one Mac, and shells out to the
#   now-private scripts/mirror-backup.sh — its ProgramArguments is a
#   `$HOME`-relative path, not a literal absolute one, but the relative part
#   still names the owner's own personal directory taxonomy in full, and
#   the whole file has no public value once mirror-backup.sh is gone
#   (review finding F2 on PR #457 corrected this comment's earlier,
#   inaccurate "absolute home-directory path" claim; review finding G1 on
#   the same PR then caught that F2's own fix had quoted that taxonomy
#   verbatim right here — removed, not repeated).
# - scripts/tests/bootstrap-docs.test.sh is a regression test for
#   docs/operations/beads-backup-and-restore.md's own Bootstrap section
#   content (hooksPath line, no hardcoded paths, the bb96v note) — it
#   hard-fails with "no doc at ..." the moment that doc is export-ignored,
#   because it is testing a file that no longer exists to test.
# - scripts/tests/pre-push-hook-stderr.test.sh copies the REAL
#   scripts/backup-beads.sh into its fixture to prove backup-beads.sh's
#   "REFUSING TO BACK UP" diagnostic reaches stderr through the pre-push
#   hook — a scenario that can only occur where backup-beads.sh exists, i.e.
#   never in a public clone. The hook's OTHER, public-relevant behavior —
#   staying silent when backup-beads.sh or .beads/ is absent — is already
#   covered by scripts/tests/git-hooks.test.sh case (c), which does not
#   depend on the real file (it writes its own stub) and keeps shipping.
scripts/launchd/app.dohflow.mirror-backup.plist export-ignore
scripts/tests/bootstrap-docs.test.sh export-ignore
scripts/tests/pre-push-hook-stderr.test.sh export-ignore
